WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.901 --> 00:00:02.067
-Welcome to the show.

00:00:02.067 --> 00:00:04.133
I'm so happy to to meet you.
I'm a big fan.

00:00:04.133 --> 00:00:06.033
I listen to your stuff.
You're fantastic.

00:00:06.033 --> 00:00:07.934
-Thank you.
I'm a huge fan of you, Jimmy.

00:00:07.934 --> 00:00:10.000
-Oh. Thank you. I mean --
I mean, "Call Her Daddy."

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.367
This is the thing.
Everyone is talking about this.

00:00:12.367 --> 00:00:14.601
Your interview skills
are fantastic.

00:00:14.601 --> 00:00:18.033
You get people to do stuff and
get into stories that I'm like,

00:00:18.033 --> 00:00:20.367
"How did she get
people to do that?"

00:00:20.367 --> 00:00:22.734
Time 100 Next just named you
on their list

00:00:22.734 --> 00:00:24.968
in the top 100 right there.
So congratulations on that.

00:00:24.968 --> 00:00:28.434
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:28.434 --> 00:00:30.334
How does it all, uh...

00:00:30.334 --> 00:00:31.767
How's it --
How's it all feeling?

00:00:31.767 --> 00:00:33.067
-It feels surreal.

00:00:33.067 --> 00:00:35.133
Like, I still feel like the girl
from Pennsylvania,

00:00:35.133 --> 00:00:37.601
like, that's awkward
with my braces in the basement,

00:00:37.601 --> 00:00:39.000
just, like, trying to make it.
-Yeah.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:40.634
-It's very surreal,
but I'm just so happy

00:00:40.634 --> 00:00:42.634
that it's happening.
And it's happening.

00:00:42.634 --> 00:00:45.501
-Your --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:45.501 --> 00:00:48.534
Your bigger news is that
you got engaged this year.

00:00:48.534 --> 00:00:50.901
-I did.
-Congratulations on this.

00:00:50.901 --> 00:00:53.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:55.100
But wait till you hear this.
The proposal

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:57.534
was pretty elaborate,
and I kind of --

00:00:57.534 --> 00:00:59.267
I can't even believe
that this is a real thing.

00:00:59.267 --> 00:01:02.467
But dreams come true. This is --
This is what I wish I did.

00:01:02.467 --> 00:01:04.000
But please walk us
through what he did.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:07.100
-Okay. Well, just to, like,
set the ground here,

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:09.434
I was the girl
that never thought

00:01:09.434 --> 00:01:11.801
she was going to get married.
Like, I had no interest.

00:01:11.801 --> 00:01:13.467
I never had the Pinterest board.

00:01:13.467 --> 00:01:15.601
I don't even I still don't even
know what my dress will be.

00:01:15.601 --> 00:01:17.934
Like, there is no vision, Jimmy.
Okay?

00:01:17.934 --> 00:01:19.667
So we're starting with nothing.

00:01:19.667 --> 00:01:22.000
-No Pinterest board.
-Yes, there is nothing. Okay?

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:24.267
So, I remember --
And I think it was because

00:01:24.267 --> 00:01:26.934
I was nervous that it threatened
my independence as a woman.

00:01:26.934 --> 00:01:29.701
And so that changed, obviously,
when I met Matt.

00:01:29.701 --> 00:01:31.901
And from the very beginning
of our relationship,

00:01:31.901 --> 00:01:33.701
I'm like, "We are
never getting married.

00:01:33.701 --> 00:01:36.300
We are life partners, okay?"
And he's like, "Okay.

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:39.000
Oh, my God, you're wacky."
And then I will never forget.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:41.300
I sat him down at a dinner
at Giorgio Baldi in L.A.

00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:43.934
and I was like, "Matt,
I have to tell you something."

00:01:43.934 --> 00:01:47.334
And he's like, "What?"
And I'm like, "You can do it."

00:01:47.334 --> 00:01:49.100
He's like, "I can do what?"

00:01:49.100 --> 00:01:51.801
And I'm like, "You can propose.
We can get married."

00:01:51.801 --> 00:01:54.367
And he's like -- he's elated.
Like, he's so happy.

00:01:54.367 --> 00:01:55.901
And it was
such a cute moment.

00:01:55.901 --> 00:01:57.501
And then a couple months later,

00:01:57.501 --> 00:02:00.701
he did it in the most
romantic possible way.

00:02:00.701 --> 00:02:03.634
I mean, Matt produces Y.A. films
for a living, so this --

00:02:03.634 --> 00:02:05.367
I felt like I was in a movie.
Okay?

00:02:05.367 --> 00:02:08.133
I got home,
I walk in, and Adele

00:02:08.133 --> 00:02:09.801
is playing all
throughout our house.

00:02:09.801 --> 00:02:14.267
Every square inch of my home
has candles all over it,

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:17.334
and there is a video of him
that basically says,

00:02:17.334 --> 00:02:20.067
follow the scavenger hunt,
and you will come find me.

00:02:20.067 --> 00:02:23.767
And every room in our home.
He had picture frames of themes,

00:02:23.767 --> 00:02:26.033
so the kitchen was filled with
all picture frames

00:02:26.033 --> 00:02:28.968
of our firsts -- the first trip
that he said, "I love you,"

00:02:28.968 --> 00:02:30.133
the first time
we went to Hawaii,

00:02:30.133 --> 00:02:31.267
the first time
he met my parents.

00:02:31.267 --> 00:02:32.801
Like, it was so touching.

00:02:32.801 --> 00:02:35.467
And then at the end, once I went
through the scavenger hunt,

00:02:35.467 --> 00:02:38.367
I saw him with
our two dogs in tuxedos

00:02:38.367 --> 00:02:40.100
underneath this, like, gazebo,

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:42.400
and he got down on one knee,
and it was perfect!

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:43.567
Oh, my God!

00:02:43.567 --> 00:02:46.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:49.100
Now, are people upset with Matt?

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:50.234
Are people mad at Matt and go,

00:02:50.234 --> 00:02:51.901
"Hey, dude,
calm it down a little bit"?

00:02:51.901 --> 00:02:53.667
-It was pretty --
It was pretty crazy.

00:02:53.667 --> 00:02:55.834
I remember reading on Twitter,
and men were like,

00:02:55.834 --> 00:02:58.167
"Matt, Matt,
can we tone it down?"

00:02:58.167 --> 00:02:59.534
Like, because girlfriends
are like,

00:02:59.534 --> 00:03:01.033
"Oh, I'm showing
my boyfriend this."

00:03:01.033 --> 00:03:02.601
Alex being like,
"I expect nothing less."

00:03:02.601 --> 00:03:05.934
And I was like, "Let's go!"
-Yeah.

00:03:05.934 --> 00:03:07.601
Congratulations.
That's the way to do it.

00:03:07.601 --> 00:03:10.000
That's awesome. I want to talk
about your new tour,

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:11.734
by the way, as well,
because you're going on

00:03:11.734 --> 00:03:13.567
this tour
called The Unwell Tour,

00:03:13.567 --> 00:03:15.801
and you're going to put some

00:03:15.801 --> 00:03:18.434
bachelorette-party vibes
into this tour.

00:03:18.434 --> 00:03:20.434
But explain to me what this tour
is so people know,

00:03:20.434 --> 00:03:21.567
fans of you will know.

00:03:21.567 --> 00:03:24.200
-So, what I will say
is, obviously,

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:27.300
because it's bachelorette-themed
and this is network television,

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:30.167
Jimmy, I can't -- I can't go
into too much detail,

00:03:30.167 --> 00:03:33.467
but what I will say is,
I have never been

00:03:33.467 --> 00:03:35.100
live in person with my fans.

00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:37.367
I call them the Daddy Gang.
Love you. Shout-out Daddy Gang!

00:03:37.367 --> 00:03:39.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:42.701
And I always try to do things
and, like, flip it on its head.

00:03:42.701 --> 00:03:44.133
Like, how can I reinvent
something?

00:03:44.133 --> 00:03:46.667
How can I think of something
different to give my audience?

00:03:46.667 --> 00:03:48.067
And when you think
of a podcast tour,

00:03:48.067 --> 00:03:49.868
you think,
"I'm gonna do this.

00:03:49.868 --> 00:03:51.601
We're gonna sit for an hour
and a half, we're gonna chat,

00:03:51.601 --> 00:03:53.367
we're going to talk."
Absolutely not.

00:03:53.367 --> 00:03:55.767
Absolutely not.
To give you a little taste,

00:03:55.767 --> 00:03:57.601
my lighting team came up to me,
and they said,

00:03:57.601 --> 00:04:01.000
"Alex, we have worked
on Broadway shows before, babe.

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:04.167
Okay? This show
has more lighting cues

00:04:04.167 --> 00:04:07.000
than some Broadway shows,"
and I'm like, "Let's go!"

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:09.100
So it's gonna be amazing.
I'm really excited.

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:10.601
I'm really excited
for my fans to see it.

00:04:10.601 --> 00:04:12.067
And I'm not going to lie,
I'm nervous

00:04:12.067 --> 00:04:14.167
because I've never
done something live.

00:04:14.167 --> 00:04:15.634
But it feels right.
It feels right.

00:04:15.634 --> 00:04:18.100
-Oh, that's great.
I know you're coming --

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:19.734
coming to the Theater
at the Garden, too,

00:04:19.734 --> 00:04:21.100
here in New York.
-Yeah. You're gonna come, right?

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:22.767
-I will totally be there.
Are you kidding me?

00:04:22.767 --> 00:04:24.067
What, are you kidding me?
-Absolutely.

00:04:24.067 --> 00:04:25.767
-What is it? Five years now
you're celebrating?

00:04:25.767 --> 00:04:27.501
-Five years.
-Congratulations, pal.

00:04:27.501 --> 00:04:30.767
Really. Well done.
I -- I love it.

00:04:30.767 --> 00:04:33.000
It's so good.
Do you hear from people?

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:36.567
Do people come up to you and go,
"Hey, you changed my life," or,

00:04:36.567 --> 00:04:38.934
"Thank you for doing that thing.
I didn't think of it that way"?

00:04:38.934 --> 00:04:41.400
What is the best compliment?
-I've got it for you.

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:43.834
Okay. One time,
I'm standing in CVS,

00:04:43.834 --> 00:04:45.467
and this girl comes up to me,
and she's like,

00:04:45.467 --> 00:04:47.367
"Alex,
I have to tell you a story,"

00:04:47.367 --> 00:04:49.434
and I'm like, "Okay.
Tell me the story."

00:04:49.434 --> 00:04:51.167
She's like, "I had a man
come up to me,

00:04:51.167 --> 00:04:53.434
and he was like,
'I hate Alex Cooper.'"

00:04:53.434 --> 00:04:54.767
And she's like,
"What do you mean?

00:04:54.767 --> 00:04:56.501
Why do you hate Alex Cooper?"
And he's like,

00:04:56.501 --> 00:05:00.834
"She is making women
way too confident."

00:05:00.834 --> 00:05:03.634
And I'm like, "Oh, my God.
I can retire now."

00:05:03.634 --> 00:05:05.334
Like, it's such a cool moment

00:05:05.334 --> 00:05:08.467
to realize that women
actually come to my show

00:05:08.467 --> 00:05:10.067
and can feel better
about themselves.

00:05:10.067 --> 00:05:12.067
I've had women stop me
in the street and be like,

00:05:12.067 --> 00:05:13.634
"I got out of
an abusive relationship

00:05:13.634 --> 00:05:14.601
because of the show."

00:05:14.601 --> 00:05:16.300
"I went in and advocated
for myself

00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:17.567
and got that raise I wanted."

00:05:17.567 --> 00:05:20.234
Like, it's a community
that has been built

00:05:20.234 --> 00:05:22.133
with a bunch of women
that are like-minded,

00:05:22.133 --> 00:05:23.634
and I'm so proud of it,

00:05:23.634 --> 00:05:25.200
and it's just going
to keep going.

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:27.234
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:27.234 --> 00:05:28.734
I think it's awesome
that you're doing that.

00:05:28.734 --> 00:05:31.567
-Thank you.
Thank you.

00:05:31.567 --> 00:05:33.234
-People --
Today is Halloween,

00:05:33.234 --> 00:05:35.534
and people are dressing up
as you, by the way.

00:05:35.534 --> 00:05:37.501
I saw a lot online.
There being you for Halloween.

00:05:37.501 --> 00:05:39.434
Does that feel odd?

00:05:39.434 --> 00:05:41.334
-It's a little odd.
But what I will say is, like,

00:05:41.334 --> 00:05:42.567
I'm looking out for the girlies.

00:05:42.567 --> 00:05:44.000
Like, if you're gonna
dress up like me,

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:46.667
obviously, if I was actually
wearing what I wanted to be

00:05:46.667 --> 00:05:48.133
in right now,
every single Daddy Gang

00:05:48.133 --> 00:05:50.767
knows I'd be in sweatpants
and a hoodie and my messy bun,

00:05:50.767 --> 00:05:51.968
and that is what
they're wearing.

00:05:51.968 --> 00:05:53.634
You just got to throw
on a sweatsuit

00:05:53.634 --> 00:05:55.300
and a messy bun, and you're
like, "I'm Alex Cooper."

00:05:55.300 --> 00:05:56.934
-There you go.
So that's a good costume.

00:05:56.934 --> 00:05:58.367
-There we go.

00:05:58.367 --> 00:06:02.901
-But I also know your your dog
Henry dresses up every year.

00:06:02.901 --> 00:06:04.667
-He does.
-And I've heard --

00:06:04.667 --> 00:06:07.167
Look at this cute dog.
People recognize this dog.

00:06:07.167 --> 00:06:09.334
-This is Cindy Lou Who
right here. Okay?

00:06:09.334 --> 00:06:11.901
-I mean, stop it.
He's so cute.

00:06:11.901 --> 00:06:14.067
And people, actually,
they come up to him

00:06:14.067 --> 00:06:15.367
on the street and like,
and they're like,

00:06:15.367 --> 00:06:17.467
"Oh, you're Henry."
-They say, "Oh, my God, Alex,

00:06:17.467 --> 00:06:18.767
I didn't notice you at first
because I --

00:06:18.767 --> 00:06:20.701
but I saw Henry, and then
I was like, 'Oh, it's you.'"

00:06:20.701 --> 00:06:22.801
Yeah. They look for Henry.
I'm like, "Okay."

00:06:22.801 --> 00:06:24.400
-Yeah, well, I thought --
I was like,

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:26.901
"What is Henry going to be
this year for Halloween?"

00:06:26.901 --> 00:06:28.534
and you were gonna tell me
and show a picture,

00:06:28.534 --> 00:06:31.267
but then you're going to --
again, you're upping the game

00:06:31.267 --> 00:06:33.133
and doing something
that's something different.

00:06:33.133 --> 00:06:34.801
You actually brought
Henry here in person.

00:06:34.801 --> 00:06:36.901
-Mm-hmm.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:36.901 --> 00:06:38.200
I did.
-Can we bring him out?

00:06:38.200 --> 00:06:39.968
-Can I go get him?
-Let's go get Henry.

00:06:39.968 --> 00:06:41.000
-Henry!

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:42.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:42.834 --> 00:06:43.968
-Hi, buba.
-Henry.

00:06:43.968 --> 00:06:45.000
-Come here.

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:47.667
[ Cheers and applause ]
Come here.

00:06:47.667 --> 00:06:48.701
Come here.

00:06:48.701 --> 00:06:52.234
-Oh, my gosh.
Henry.

00:06:52.234 --> 00:06:54.133
-Hi, buba!
-Henry.

00:06:54.133 --> 00:06:55.801
-Hi!
Oh. Hi, Henry. Are you --

00:06:55.801 --> 00:06:57.200
Oh. Thank you.
I don't have a treat yet,

00:06:57.200 --> 00:06:59.100
but you're a nice burrito.
Henry.

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:00.801
-Yeah, he's a little burrito.

00:07:00.801 --> 00:07:02.734
You guys, I may have put
the costume on wrong,

00:07:02.734 --> 00:07:05.033
but we're going to pretend
that didn't happen. Sit.

00:07:05.033 --> 00:07:08.367
It's okay, Jimmy, he'll give you
his paw if you ask for his paw,

00:07:08.367 --> 00:07:09.701
but he can only
give his left one,

00:07:09.701 --> 00:07:10.901
so, like, you know,
be easy on him.

00:07:10.901 --> 00:07:12.100
-Oh, should we do it
over this way then?

00:07:12.100 --> 00:07:13.701
-Yeah, yeah, yeah. Sit.
-Right. Here we go. Sit.

00:07:13.701 --> 00:07:15.100
-Sit. Paw.

00:07:15.100 --> 00:07:16.767
Good boy!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:16.767 --> 00:07:19.467
-Oh, my God!
Henry, wait.

00:07:19.467 --> 00:07:20.868
You want me to do it?
Let me do it.

00:07:20.868 --> 00:07:22.033
-Yeah, yeah, give another one.

00:07:22.033 --> 00:07:23.567
You got it, you got it.
-I want a Henry --

00:07:23.567 --> 00:07:26.033
-Henry, sit. Paw.
Ask for paw first.

00:07:26.033 --> 00:07:28.334
-Paw.
-Good, baby.

00:07:28.334 --> 00:07:29.868
-Oh, what a good boy!

00:07:29.868 --> 00:07:30.934
Happy Halloween.

00:07:30.934 --> 00:07:33.467
Happy Halloween!
Alex Cooper!

00:07:33.467 --> 00:07:34.968
New episodes of "Call Her Daddy"

00:07:34.968 --> 00:07:37.734
stream every Wednesday
on Spotify.

00:07:37.734 --> 00:07:40.334
We'll be right back with a
performance from Depeche Mode.

00:07:40.334 --> 00:07:42.133
Stick around.
You want another one?

